__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
# Parallel coverage fragments. pytest-cov under pytest-xdist writes one
# `.coverage.<host>.<pid>.<random>` per worker into the rootdir, and the exact
# name `.coverage` above does not match them. Untracked, they make
# `git status --porcelain` report a dirty tree whose path COUNT changes while
# the suite is still running -- which broke
# test_two_runs_differ_only_in_the_timestamp, since generate_evidence.py
# measures that count and two runs then legitimately disagreed. The generator
# was not non-deterministic; its input was moving underneath it.
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
.mutmut-cache
.hypothesis/
.venv/
venv/
reports/
node_modules/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# Scratch git worktrees created for isolated agent runs. They are full
# checkouts of this repository living inside it; committing one would nest the
# tree in itself and drag whatever an agent installed there into history.
.claude/

# Local sandbox evidence. Every `make sandbox-*` run writes argv, exit codes, durations
# and captured output here. It is generated, machine-local, and regenerated on demand;
# committing it would put a second copy of run results under review alongside the
# authoritative GitHub evidence.
.evidence/

# Vite build output for the learning-canvas frontend. Generated by `npm run build`
# in frontend/, reproduced from source on demand, and uploaded from CI as a run
# artifact rather than committed. node_modules/ above already covers the install.
frontend/dist/
# `tsc -b` incremental state. Regenerated by every typecheck and build; committing it
# means reviewing a machine's build cache.
frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Canvas browser-harness output. Every run writes measured metrics per project
# here; the numbers belong in the phase report, which quotes them, rather than
# in history, where a machine's timings would be reviewed as if they were code.
frontend/e2e/report/
.DS_Store
screenshots/
